«
@@ ============================================================
@@ XYZtoLLH — Earth-centred, Earth-fixed coordinates (ECEF) to
@@ geodetic latitude, longitude and height on the WGS-84 ellipsoid.
@@ B. R. Bowring, "Transformation from spatial to geographical
@@ coordinates", Survey Review 23(181), 1976; one pass is accurate to
@@ better than a millimetre for points near the Earth's surface.
@@
@@ Input : X Y Z — plain numbers are metres; lengths with a unit are
@@         accepted.
@@ Output: φ λ h — latitude and longitude (East positive) in degrees,
@@         height above the ellipsoid in metres.
@@ Angle mode and angle units setting are restored before returning.
@@ ============================================================

  3 →LIST
  « IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN 1_m CONVERT UVAL END »
  MAP LIST→ DROP
  Ⓒa♁GPS →Num UVAL Ⓒf♁GPS →Num Ⓒe12♁GPS →Num Ⓒe22♁GPS →Num
  'AngleMode' RCL 'SetAngleUnits' RCL
  RAD NoAngleUnits
  → xx yy zz axa fla ecc ecp amode aunits
  «
    'axa*(1-fla)' EVAL '√(xx²+yy²)' EVAL
    → bxa pp
    «
      '(zz*axa)∠(pp*bxa)' EVAL
      → qq
      «
        '(zz+ecp*bxa*SIN(qq)³)∠(pp-ecc*axa*COS(qq)³)' EVAL
        → lat
        «
          lat 180 * Ⓒπ →Num / 1_° *
          '(yy)∠(xx)' EVAL 180 * Ⓒπ →Num / 1_° *
          'pp/COS(lat)-axa/√(1-ecc*SIN(lat)²)' EVAL 1_m *
        »
      »
    »
    amode EVAL IF aunits THEN SetAngleUnits ELSE NoAngleUnits END
  »
»
